Perfect! The implementation is complete and verified:

✅ **`slugify` function implemented correctly** in `textkit/core.py`:
  - Lowercases text using `text.lower()`
  - Replaces runs of non-alphanumeric characters with single dashes using `re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', text)`
  - Strips leading/trailing dashes with `text.strip('-')`

✅ **Exported properly** from `textkit/__init__.py`

✅ **Comprehensive unit tests** added covering:
  - Basic slug conversion ("Hello World" → "hello-world")
  - Multiple spaces/special characters
  - Edge cases (empty strings, only dashes, only spaces)

✅ **All tests pass**: 3/3 tests successful with no errors

